HW TX Engine Active
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ Descriptors are transmitted │
│ Hardware generates TX IRQs │
└─────────────┬───────────────┘
              │
              ▼
       CPSW TX Interrupt Handler
       (cpsw_tx_interrupt)
       ┌─────────────────────────────┐
       │ 1️⃣ Disable tx_en (writel 0) │
       │    - Stop TX DMA engine      │
       │    - Prevent new TX IRQs     │
       │ 2️⃣ Send EOI to hardware     │
       │ 3️⃣ Possibly disable Linux   │
       │    IRQ line (quirk)         │
       │ 4️⃣ Schedule NAPI (napi_tx) │
       └─────────────────────────────┘
              │
              ▼
       Softirq: NAPI Polling
       (cpsw_tx_poll called via napi_poll)
       ┌─────────────────────────────┐
       │ 1️⃣ Process up to `budget`   │
       │    completed TX descriptors │
       │ 2️⃣ Call cpsw_tx_handler     │
       │    - Free SKBs / XDP frames │
       │    - Update TX stats        │
       │    - Wake TX queue if needed│
       │ 3️⃣ If all descriptors done  │
       │    - napi_complete          │
       │    - Re-enable tx_en (0xff) │
       │    - Re-enable Linux IRQ    │
       └─────────────────────────────┘
              │
              ▼
       TX Engine Resumes
       ┌─────────────────────────────┐
       │ HW TX engine ready to send  │
       │ next descriptors             │
       │ IRQs can fire again          │
       └─────────────────────────────┘

